<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<div>
  <p>
    Controller Clock shows the Jenkins controller time in the global header.
  </p>
  <p>
    The display is synced from Jenkins, so it reflects controller time rather than the browser clock.
  </p>

  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Displays controller time in the Jenkins header</li>
    <li>Updates from Jenkins on a refresh interval</li>
    <li>Uses controller time, not browser time</li>
    <li>Shows the active Jenkins timezone in the tooltip</li>
    <li>No plugin-specific configuration</li>
    <li>No telemetry or outbound requests</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Jenkins 2.541.3 or newer</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Usage</h2>
  <p>
    Once installed, the clock is visible in the Jenkins header.
    Hover over it to see the full time and the timezone Jenkins is using.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and Network Behavior</h2>
  <p>
    Controller Clock is a local Jenkins feature. It does not send telemetry, analytics, or other outbound Internet traffic.
    The browser only calls the Jenkins controller on the same origin to sync clock state.
  </p>
</div>
